{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the harmonic mean of 10 and 20.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378c2f50c9975c17b0c08c1bf179db7c9057ce56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\, 15\\quad\\mathrm{(B)}\\, \\frac{40}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"116\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Harmonic_mean\" title=\"Harmonic mean\">harmonic mean</a> of two numbers is the reciprocal of the mean of the reciprocals of the two numbers.  The reciprocals of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413ef40e68bba048027f5985031889e344c3bf5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfde23c6a2e199961e2b2d9404f38ba95f184e5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"21\" /> and the mean of the two is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b440c76219942559227bae9adf8cbb475db925d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac3{40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"21\" />, so the harmonic mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95ff3d80bfc7a6f0d77d1f31466b36b1308dd2d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\tfrac{40}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <